Z||000000||fotofrank||08-02-2000||11:04 PM||||OK hereis one for all you 4 banger experts.<BR>The '84 iron Duke has a wedge shaped pice of metal in the intake right below the TBI. Is this a "restrictor plate" or a device to direct air and fuel into the head? I installed my Holley TBI but got it used with no instructions. The books I have do not mention the said pise of metal. I await the wisdom of the forum. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE 2M4<BR>http://fotofrank.homestead.com/foto1.html||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||08-03-2000||08:53 PM||||It's not a restrictor. I believe it's there to improve air flow to #'s 1 & 4. There's no really usefull info about it.<P>You may have to remove it if it blocks the new TBI throttle plate. Otherwise leave it.||||reg||1
